 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (HVAC)",
 "applies_to": "Vacon 100, Vacon 100 FLOW and Vacon 100 HVAC AC drives using the built-in RS-485 port (BACnet MS/TP) or the built-in Ethernet port (BACnet IP).",
 "summary": "Vacon 100 family drives (now Danfoss) have BACnet MS/TP on the RS-485 terminals and BACnet IP on the Ethernet port, both built in. The object list is Binary Values for drive status, run/stop, direction, reset, stop modes and fieldbus control-word bits, and Analog Values for monitors, the speed reference (% of nominal), limits, ramps, process data, AnyParam access and the fixed control/status words.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "0 = use the number read from the drive (shown in the monitor menu)",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "From the Vacon 100 Internal BACnet Installation Manual DPD00091B (Danfoss AN361179477697en-000101), Tables 14-15 (PDF pp32-34).",
  "Fieldbus must be the remote control place (P3.2.1 Rem. Ctrl. Place) for BV 15 and AV 24 to take effect.",
  "BV 7-14 and AV 15-22 / AV 30-33 are process data whose meaning depends on the application.",
  "AV 36/AV 37 are IEEE-754 floats; binary coding works only for values without decimals.",
  "The control word (AV 36) uses bit 0 start/stop, bit 1 direction, bit 2 fault reset; the status word (AV 38) bit 0 ready, 1 run, 2 direction, 3 fault, 4 alarm, 5 at reference, 6 zero speed.",
  "High and low limits of the objects come from the drive application."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Vacon 100 AC drives, Internal BACnet Installation Manual",
  "doc_number": "DPD00091B (AN361179477697en-000101)",
  "revision_date": "2013-06-04",
  "url": "https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/277119/AN361179477697en-000101.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Select the BACnet protocol on RS-485 (M5.8) or Ethernet (M5.9), set the MS/TP MAC address, baud rate and instance (P5.8.3.1) or the IP settings and P5.9.3.1.3 Protocol in use = 1, and make Fieldbus the remote control place (P3.2.1). Then command BV 15 run/stop (or AV 36 control word) and AV 24 speed reference, and read BV 1, AV 1 and the fault points.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 15",
    "name": "Run/Stop CMD",
    "why": "Run/stop command (1 = run)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 24",
    "name": "Speed Reference",
    "why": "Speed reference, % of nominal speed"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 17",
    "name": "Reset Fault",
    "why": "Resets the active fault"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 1",
    "name": "Run/Stop State",
    "why": "Running status"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1",
    "name": "Output Frequency",
    "why": "Output frequency, Hz"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 5",
    "name": "Motor Current",
    "why": "Motor current, A"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3",
    "name": "Load (power)",
    "why": "Motor shaft power, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 3",
    "name": "Fault State",
    "why": "Any active drive fault"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 23",
    "name": "Active Fault Code",
    "why": "Which fault is active"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Make Fieldbus the remote control place (Main Menu > Parameters > Start/Stop Setup > P3.2.1 Rem. Ctrl. Place) and choose the fieldbus as the reference source (M3.3). The manual's quick test writes AV 36 control word 0 then 1 to start, AV 24 = 50 for 50 % speed, and 0 to stop.",
  "heartbeat": "MS/TP: P5.8.3.1.5 Communication time-out (0-65535 s, default 10, 0 = off) raises a communication error if the drive is sole master for that long. BACnet IP: P5.9.3.1.2 Communication time-out (default 0 = not used) is the longest allowed gap between UDP packets from the master; losing the Ethernet link faults at once even with 0.",
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "MS/TP: P5.8.3.1.1 baud rate (1 = 9600 default, 2 = 19200, 3 = 38400, 4 = 76800), P5.8.3.1.2 autobauding, P5.8.3.1.3 MAC address 1-127 (default 1).",
   "P5.8.3.1.4 / P5.9.3.1.1 Instance number: 0 (default) uses a number read from the drive, shown in the monitor menu; any other value is used as is.",
   "BACnet IP: P5.9.1.1 IP address mode (default 1 = DHCP with AutoIP; 0 = fixed, default 192.168.0.10); P5.9.3.1.3 Protocol in use = 1 turns BACnet IP on.",
   "BACnet IP: P5.9.3.1.4-6 set a BBMD IP, port and time to live for foreign-device registration.",
   "Terminate the first and last drive on the MS/TP segment.",
   "PICS lists DS-RP-B, DS-RPM-B, DS-WP-B, DS-WPM-B, DM-DDB-B and DM-DOB-B; the drive is a B-ASC."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "BV 15 run/stop only works when the fieldbus is the active control place.",
   "Process data objects depend on the drive application; check the application manual before mapping them.",
   "BV 18-22 stop modes and BV 23/24 BusCtrl/BusRef are commandable control-word bits; leave them alone unless needed."
  ]
 },
